        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: 1920 Politics, Jim Crow, Republican political strategy, American Anglo-Saxon values\n- Places: Territory of Hawaii, State of Hawaii, United States\n- Topics: white racial authority, Hawaii political history\n\nFacts:\n- The Territory of Hawaii was an organized incorporated territory of the United States from August 12, 1898, to August 21, 1959.\n- On August 21, 1959, the Territory of Hawaii was admitted to the Union as the fiftieth U.S. state, the State of Hawaii.\n- Around 1930, 1920 Politics in Hawaii was also referred to as Jim Crow.\n- 1920 Politics was a Republican political strategy in the Territory of Hawaii that aimed to reassert white racial authority and promote American Anglo-Saxon values.",
